---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../consts';
---

<Legal
	title="Disclosures"
	description="What Stockpile bags are and aren't, what you own when you buy xStocks and PreStocks, and the risks of on-chain trading."
	updated={LEGAL_UPDATED}
>
	<p class="lead">The plain-English version of what you're buying, what you're not, and what can go wrong.</p>

	<h2 id="not-advice">Not investment advice</h2>
	<p>
		Bags, weights, stories, and evidence are editorial or public-record information. Nothing here is a recommendation to buy or sell
		anything, and no performance is implied.
	</p>

	<h2 id="issuers">Issuer products</h2>
	<p>
		xStocks are tokenized certificates issued by Backed that track listed equities. PreStocks are SPV-based tokens issued by
		PreStocks that reference private-company valuations. Holders do not own the underlying shares and have no voting, dividend, or
		information rights.
	</p>
	<p>
		Each issuer sets its own eligibility rules. xStocks are restricted in some jurisdictions, and PreStocks are not available to U.S.
		persons. Learn more at <a href="https://xstocks.fi/products" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">xstocks.fi</a> and
		<a href="https://prestocks.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">prestocks.com</a>.
	</p>

	<h2 id="liquidity">Thin liquidity is possible</h2>
	<p>
		On-chain quotes can carry measurable price impact, and token prices can diverge from exchange or issuer prices, especially outside
		market hours. Total loss is possible.
	</p>

	<h2 id="disclosure-bags">Disclosure bags lag</h2>
	<p>
		STOCK Act filings arrive 30 to 45 days after a trade, report value ranges rather than exact amounts, and include spouse trades.
		Disclosure bags are built from public records. They are not a managed or live portfolio, and no member of Congress endorses or
		is affiliated with Stockpile.
	</p>

	<h2 id="non-custodial">Non-custodial</h2>
	<p>
		Trades are Jupiter swaps signed by your own Privy embedded wallet after the transaction is inspected on your device. Stockpile
		never holds keys or funds, and it only relays transactions your wallet has already signed.
	</p>

	<p class="callout">
		For the full details, read our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, including the sections on risks and restricted
		jurisdictions, and our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>
</Legal>
